    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG3:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "He gathered the children of Ammon and Amalek to himself; and he went and struck Israel, and they possessed the city of palm trees."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG5:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Those whose root is in Amalek came out of Ephraim, after you, Benjamin, among your peoples. Governors come down out of Machir. Those who handle the marshal’s staff came out of Zebulun."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG6:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "So it was, when Israel had sown, that the Midianites, the Amalekites, and the children of the east came up against them."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG6:33",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then all the Midianites and the Amalekites and the children of the east assembled themselves together; and they passed over, and encamped in the valley of Jezreel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG7:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "The Midianites and the Amalekites and all the children of the east lay along in the valley like locusts for multitude; and their camels were without number, as the sand which is on the seashore for multitude."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG10:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "The Sidonians also, and the Amalekites, and the Maonites, oppressed you; and you cried to me, and I saved you out of their hand."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG12:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abdon the son of Hillel the Pirathonite died, and was buried in Pirathon in the land of Ephraim, in the hill country of the Amalekites."
      }
    ],
